 "sources": [
  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/content/dam/boeing/v2/airports/acaps/777X_Rev_G.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, 777-9 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (D6-86073 Rev G, September 2025, preliminary information), 2.2.1 General Dimensions: Model 777-9, and 2.7.1 Door Locations",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "The outlines are the 777-9's (shapes/B779.json, tools/trace/b779/) with the 777-8's two fuselage plugs taken out (tools/trace/b778/): the same wing, GE9X nacelles, tail and fuselage section, which every Boeing 777-8 source says it shares. Its door table (2.7.1) places door 3 (42.72 m on the 777-9), which the sheet's side view hides behind the flaps. Fuselage height, width, tailplane span and engine position are the 777-9's printed figures. Its table puts all three lower cargo doors, the bulk door included, on the right (as D6-58329-2's 777-200LR/-300ER cargo-door figure draws them)."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/resources/boeingdotcom/commercial/airports/acaps/777_8F_Brochure.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, 777-8F Airport Compatibility Brochure (June 2023, preliminary), size comparisons, door location comparisons, landing gear footprint",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "The 777-8 passenger aircraft has the 777-8F's fuselage length (Boeing, 2023). Overall length 232 ft 6 in (70.86 m), span 235 ft 5 in (71.76 m), wheelbase 93 ft 10 in (106 ft 1 in on the 777-9): the plugs, 3.734 m ahead of the main gear and 2.133 m behind it. Door 1 at 22 ft 2 in and the forward cargo door at 38 ft 9 in, as the 777-9's; the lower aft cargo door at 157 ft 9 in, the 777-9's large one less both plugs."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://www.boeing.com/commercial/777x",
   "title": "Boeing, 777X (boeing.com product page): 777-8 and 777-9 dimensions",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "777-8 length 232 ft 6 in (70.9 m), 777-9 251 ft 9 in (76.7 m); the same wingspan (235 ft 5 in extended, 212 ft 9 in folded) and height (64 ft 1 in)."
  },
  {
   "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20230213094036/https://www.boeing.com/resources/boeingdotcom/commercial/airports/acaps/777Xbrochure.pdf",
   "title": "Boeing, 777X Airport Compatibility Brochure (May 2015, preliminary), 777-8X general arrangement and servicing arrangement",
   "accessed": "2026-11-15",
   "note": "The 777-8 as first designed (69.8 m, 1.07 m shorter behind the wing than today's; the same 93 ft 10 in wheelbase). Its servicing plan places door 2 at its passenger bridge (about 19.3 m from the nose) and draws door tabs on both sides at about 38.9, 43.2 and 54.9 m: the 777-9's door 3, optional exit and door 4 with the plugs out, so the forward plug is ahead of door 2 and the aft one between door 3 and the exit. Read off a small plan view, to about 0.3 m. The door positions here follow from that, not from a 777-8 door table (none is published): confidence low."
  }
 ],
